          selection: {
            final_read_ids: [Array],
            summary: 'Fix #1241: ensure the first input position is a valid match position even on first usage of a context. Root cause: ZSTD_window_init zero-initializes the ZSTD_window_t, leaving base/dictBase at NULL/0 with dictLimit == lowLimit == 0, so indices can reference position 0, which is never a valid source byte (base points at the first byte; valid indices start at 1). Fix (in lib/compress/zstd_compress_internal.h, ZSTD_window_init): start all index references at 1 — initialize window->base and window->dictBase to an empty-string anchor ((BYTE const*)""), set window->dictLimit = 1, window->lowLimit = 1, and window->nextSrc = window->base + 1. This makes position 0 invalid/unmatchable by construction for both the first block and every subsequent context reuse, while ZSTD_window_update, ZSTD_window_correctOverflow, and ZSTD_window_enforceMaxDist (which compute current = src - base and clamp lowLimit) remain consistent since dictLimit/lowLimit are simply offset by 1. Evidence: base views of zstd_compress_internal.h lines 470-529 (window init/struct definitions) and 529-739 (window_correctOverflow, window_enforceMaxDist, window_update), which are the only functions touched; LDM and MT compression paths (h1-h4) consume these windows unchanged and need no edits.',
