          selection: {
            final_read_ids: [Array],
            summary: 'Fix #1241: first input position invalid for a match on first context usage. Root cause: ZSTD_window_t is zeroed on reset, so window->base/dictBase/lowLimit/dictLimit start at 0; ZSTD_window_update() then treats the first block as starting at index 0, and index 0 is reserved as invalid (match indices are compared with >= lowLimit, so a match can falsely reference position 0 or index arithmetic underflows). The fix starts the reference index at 1: on reset/first usage initialize lowLimit = dictLimit = 1 (with base/dictBase pointing at a sentinel/empty base), so the first input byte gets index 1 and every match index >= lowLimit corresponds to a real, valid position for both first and subsequent context usages. Evidence: window state struct and invariants (h29, h30, h8, h10), ZSTD_window_update non-contiguous path computing distanceFromBase/dictLimit (h0), and compress.c reset sites that zero the matchState/window (h22, h27, h28, h3).',
            model_context_handles: [Array],
            response_capture_sha256: '295dbb0e8e837d44870faf8e0c977bd0de3cea9e69d9906bd14955e9903670cd',
