void fast_minify_twitter(State& state) {\\"},{\\"end_line\\":28,\\"path\\":\\"benchmark/bench_parse_call.cpp\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"6e3c23a0badb7200b890573410b25ca417a5e8e210823166d779c40607510fab\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"33689e31afa0b50e8e145db940f14ffcb9566d2d67f1ed4eeb4306098ff8ed4d\\",\\"start_line\\":28,\\"total_lines\\":256,\\"utf8\\":\\"    auto error = simdjson::minify(docdata.data(), docdata.size(), buffer.get(), new_length);\\"},{\\"end_line\\":38,\\"path\\":\\"benchmark/bench_parse_call.cpp\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"41111d2a4e31ad39dca629984ee5ee0e8282a4011f5bc3526283072c7aa31fa4\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"33689e31afa0b50e8e145db940f14ffcb9566d2d67f1ed4eeb4306098ff8ed4d\\",\\"start_line\\":38,\\"total_lines\\":256,\\"utf8\\":\\"BENCHMARK(fast_minify_twitter)->Repetitions(10)->ComputeStatistics(\\\\\\"max\\\\\\", [](const std::vector<double>& v) -> double {\\"},{\\"end_line\\":45,\\"path\\":\\"benchmark/bench_parse_call.cpp\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"95a54730b8dfb7437572c6d70cdc0ced9b37a2e323a34ad32ec7c61949392d4c\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"33689e31afa0b50e8e145db940f14ffcb9566d2d67f1ed4eeb4306098ff8ed4d\\",\\"start_line\\":45,\\"total_lines\\":256,\\"utf8\\":\\"static void fast_minify_gsoc(State& state) {\\"},{\\"end_line\\":58,\\"path\\":\\"benchmark/bench_parse_call.cpp\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"a61d21b3f548a00d1e25e2a1aac4be5ea5c1be8954272d964463034489810c4b\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"33689e31afa0b50e8e145db940f14ffcb9566d2d67f1ed4eeb4306098ff8ed4d\\",\\"start_line\\":58,\\"total_lines\\":256,\\"utf8\\":\\"    auto error = simdjson::minify(docdata.data(), docdata.size(), buffer.get(), new_length);\\"},{\\"end_line\\":68,\\"path\\":\\"benchmark/bench_parse_call.cpp\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"30b713718ae620dc42280663ce94202b8995d56bb6f7d23ede34b2f62f14c468\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"33689e31afa0b50e8e145db940f14ffcb9566d2d67f1ed4eeb4306098ff8ed4d\\",\\"start_line\\":68,\\"total_lines\\":256,\\"utf8\\":\\"BENCHMARK(fast_minify_gsoc)->Repetitions(10)->ComputeStatistics(\\\\\\"max\\\\\\", [](const std::vector<double>& v) -> double {\\"},{\\"end_line\\":18,\\"path\\":\\"doc/basics.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"9e42ff581624ab0f6bc665edab2ebe612eb1696c79a68d8c18da31bbe533be5d\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"aa2bee6ce5e17990204c3dc01f76a9237237836d885f939c1d159e7744e4813c\\",\\"start_line\\":18,\\"total_lines\\":1972,\\"utf8\\":\\"  - [Minifying JSON strings without parsing](#minifying-json-strings-without-parsing)\\"},{\\"end_line\\":736,\\"path\\":\\"doc/basics.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"0e83343a88c15fac3e7880f13d60414fb4cafff7dab541ed7f619914c66a8bd2\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"aa2bee6ce5e17990204c3dc01f76a9237237836d885f939c1d159e7744e4813c\\",\\"start_line\\":736,\\"total_lines\\":1972,\\"utf8\\":\\"In some cases, you may have valid JSON strings that you do not wish to parse but that you wish to minify. That is, you wish to remove all unnecessary spaces. We have a fast function for this purpose (`simdjson::minify(const char * input, size_t length, const char * output, size_t& new_length)`). This function does not validate your content, and it does not parse it.  It is much faster than parsing the string and re-serializing it in minified form (`simdjson::minify(parser.parse())`). Usage is relatively simple. You must pass an input pointer with a length parameter, as well as an output pointer and an output length parameter (by reference). The output length parameter is not read, but written to. The output pointer should point to a valid memory region that is as large as the original string length. The input pointer and input length are read, but not written to.\\"},{\\"end_line\\":746,\\"path\\":\\"doc/basics.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"cbd5023f93e5749058e7114fdd98e44e71d35bfa9069ec2ad72f9d866b0ffde0\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"aa2bee6ce5e17990204c3dc01f76a9237237836d885f939c1d159e7744e4813c\\",\\"start_line\\":746,\\"total_lines\\":1972,\\"utf8\\":\\"  auto error = simdjson::minify(some_string, length, buffer.get(), new_length);\\"},{\\"end_line\\":750,\\"path\\":\\"doc/basics.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"5b7d855a9ab11cab1fb9be1cdbcf0812439856e31dcd76dad167c3c68801a109\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"aa2bee6ce5e17990204c3dc01f76a9237237836d885f939c1d159e7744e4813c\\",\\"start_line\\":750,\\"total_lines\\":1972,\\"utf8\\":\\"Though it does not validate the JSON input, it will detect when the document ends with an unterminated string. E.g., it would refuse to minify the string `\\\\\\"this string is not terminated` because of the missing final quote.\\"},{\\"end_line\\":108,\\"path\\":\\"doc/dom.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"6ee5eb84dbb330e3b4d606760414074098eaed03bc77eb640fac161971c2a28e\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"4524a04469a0fce6db04218654f9417af1ad3e9c245529ba5d0ddab8d2fe9c6d\\",\\"start_line\\":108,\\"total_lines\\":667,\\"utf8\\":\\"* **Output to streams and strings:** Given a document or an element (or node) out of a JSON document, you can output a minified string version using the C++ stream idiom (`out << element`). You can also request the construction of a minified string version (`simdjson::minify(element)`). Numbers are serialized as 64-bit floating-point numbers (`double`).\\"},{\\"end_line\\":62,\\"path\\":\\"fuzz/CMakeLists.txt\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"a56a1a49dd8327c9610d23e7143ec731b3cdd31bc9af1f4fe453270b8a3182e9\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"5b338f5e559c91d6d92992ff73dc28b929c5cb27385968913b225edd0e8b515b\\",\\"start_line\\":62,\\"total_lines\\":75,\\"utf8\\":\\"  implement_fuzzer(fuzz_minify)          # minify *with* parsing\\"},{\\"end_line\\":63,\\"path\\":\\"fuzz/CMakeLists.txt\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"4dbba856c7cda9291d88d09b0774f81e6762d0d2c3f88031c5affd7efaa7fb97\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\