            final_read_ids: [Array],
            summary: 'Task: add DOM pretty printing (indentation fixed at four spaces) with documentation, closing #1329. The relevant base evidence is in include/simdjson/dom/serialization.h and serialization-inl.h. serialization.h (h0, h18, h20) shows the string_builder<mini_formatter> template design: a formatter parametrizes output, so prettification fits by adding a second formatter (e.g., simdjson::mini_formatter vs a pretty formatter) or by extending the public API (e.g., simdjson::to_string / simdjson::prettify) alongside the existing minified path. serialization-inl.h ranges cover the append(element/array/object/key_value_pair) implementations (h4, h21, h19, h5), the mini_formatter atom/number/string/key printers (h1, h3), and buffer/str/clear details (h7, h24, h25) needed to implement a pretty formatter with indentation, newlines, and four-space indent while reusing the existing string escaping. h8 covers the tail of serialization.h (to_string/prettify declarations area). Benchmarks and ondemand logger handles are not relevant to this change.',
