\",\\"start_line\\":44,\\"total_lines\\":76,\\"utf8\\":\\"\\\\t\\\\t<source type=\'video/mp4\' src=\'https://svelte-technology-assets.surge.sh/just-write-css.mp4\'>\\"},{\\"end_line\\":40,\\"path\\":\\"documentation/blog/2018-04-18-version-2.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"7a5ed7302b0fe2ceee09ae9cbfae13007c548111299841a8cd893ef900c3bf4e\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"a33d86076fdb77091482bd9527a64c949516b840f0038b3a505033b1d27fb6ef\\",\\"start_line\\":40,\\"total_lines\\":201,\\"utf8\\":\\"npx svelte-upgrade v2 src\\"},{\\"end_line\\":43,\\"path\\":\\"documentation/blog/2018-04-18-version-2.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"f301d5cff6a16f13f9f3fd9592515541c46eb25c522ea8ef101c1ca206d915b7\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"a33d86076fdb77091482bd9527a64c949516b840f0038b3a505033b1d27fb6ef\\",\\"start_line\\":43,\\"total_lines\\":201,\\"utf8\\":\\"This assumes any `.html` files in `src` are Svelte components. You can specify whichever directory you like, or target a different directory — for example, you\'d do `npx svelte-upgrade v2 routes` to update a [Sapper](https://sapper.svelte.technology) app.\\"},{\\"end_line\\":21,\\"path\\":\\"documentation/blog/2018-12-26-svelte-css-in-js.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"c1479195447e8e37043ddbf9d82e49f2c17cdf484df3e41a16e4cd35707ab635\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"33c80c110a170cbd999548e689a93be98fcb46a49d75c5107ca7a89bbdafd8f9\\",\\"start_line\\":21,\\"total_lines\\":28,\\"utf8\\":\\"\\\\t\\\\tsrc=\\\\\\"/repl/embed?example=blog-svelte-css-in-js\\\\\\"\\"},{\\"end_line\\":41,\\"path\\":\\"documentation/blog/2018-12-27-virtual-dom-is-pure-overhead.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"430c3971b05d781d15c1246d6397dbca27ab8d1c47e2f04eee9fbf7c90bb0a83\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"bd153122509e93817d8b6ffb21d54f01b458afdb4acef17b4660691fbcbe2255\\",\\"start_line\\":41,\\"total_lines\\":135,\\"utf8\\":\\"\\\\t<img alt=\\\\\\"Pete Hunt at JSConfEU 2013\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\"/media/rethinking-best-practices.jpg\\\\\\">\\"},{\\"end_line\\":21,\\"path\\":\\"documentation/blog/2019-01-31-svelte-on-the-changelog.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"b57408862d513772d0b15ec142423aeb0a3b0c544b31521d246898bcb558396c\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"65545dae4098a83318a9baaff6730cbb63fe5bae42575d00e3da8344e2b4ffea\\",\\"start_line\\":21,\\"total_lines\\":21,\\"utf8\\":\\"<audio data-theme=\\\\\\"night\\\\\\" style=\\\\\\"width: 100%\\\\\\" data-src=\\\\\\"https://changelog.com/podcast/332/embed\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\"https://cdn.changelog.com/uploads/podcast/332/the-changelog-332.mp3\\\\\\" preload=\\\\\\"none\\\\\\" class=\\\\\\"changelog-episode\\\\\\" controls></audio><p><a href=\\\\\\"https://changelog.com/podcast/332\\\\\\">The Changelog 332: A UI framework without the framework</a> – Listen on <a href=\\\\\\"https://changelog.com/\\\\\\">Changelog.com</a></p><script async src=\\\\\\"//cdn.changelog.com/embed.js\\\\\\"></script>\\"},{\\"end_line\\":67,\\"path\\":\\"documentation/blog/2019-04-16-svelte-for-new-developers.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"67fb862698423bf92db6181c6edd269385b1a3a59fdfd3d238f7eef22b428694\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"ddd1fb7e65bad04b53a53dc2083e37d7ed616d291c1897ec1ddd76e6338b2595\\",\\"start_line\\":67,\\"total_lines\\":95,\\"utf8\\":\\"This creates a new directory, `my-svelte-project`, adds files from the [create-vite/template-svelte](https://github.com/vitejs/vite/tree/main/packages/create-vite/template-svelte) template, and installs a number of packages from npm. Open the directory in your text editor and take a look around. The app\'s \'source code\' lives in the `src` directory, while the files your app can load are in `public`.\\"},{\\"end_line\\":79,\\"path\\":\\"documentation/blog/2019-04-16-svelte-for-new-developers.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"1da78f9b77d9d6d5f3ff89829c5fd61facf55f464fd5fce28e820f107aa9b76e\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"ddd1fb7e65bad04b