\",\\"start_line\\":44,\\"total_lines\\":76,\\"utf8\\":\\"\\\\t\\\\t<source type=\'video/mp4\' src=\'https://svelte-technology-assets.surge.sh/just-write-css.mp4\'>\\"},{\\"end_line\\":40,\\"path\\":\\"documentation/blog/2018-04-18-version-2.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"7a5ed7302b0fe2ceee09ae9cbfae13007c548111299841a8cd893ef900c3bf4e\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"a33d86076fdb77091482bd9527a64c949516b840f0038b3a505033b1d27fb6ef\\",\\"start_line\\":40,\\"total_lines\\":201,\\"utf8\\":\\"npx svelte-upgrade v2 src\\"},{\\"end_line\\":43,\\"path\\":\\"documentation/blog/2018-04-18-version-2.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"f301d5cff6a16f13f9f3fd9592515541c46eb25c522ea8ef101c1ca206d915b7\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"a33d86076fdb77091482bd9527a64c949516b840f0038b3a505033b1d27fb6ef\\",\\"start_line\\":43,\\"total_lines\\":201,\\"utf8\\":\\"This assumes any `.html` files in `src` are Svelte components. You can specify whichever directory you like, or target a different directory — for example, you\'d do `npx svelte-upgrade v2 routes` to update a [Sapper](https://sapper.svelte.technology) app.\\"},{\\"end_line\\":21,\\"path\\":\\"documentation/blog/2018-12-26-svelte-css-in-js.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"c1479195447e8e37043ddbf9d82e49f2c17cdf484df3e41a16e4cd35707ab635\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"33c80c110a170cbd999548e689a93be98fcb46a49d75c5107ca7a89bbdafd8f9\\",\\"start_line\\":21,\\"total_lines\\":28,\\"utf8\\":\\"\\\\t\\\\tsrc=\\\\\\"/repl/embed?example=blog-svelte-css-in-js\\\\\\"\\"},{\\"end_line\\":41,\\"path\\":\\"documentation/blog/2018-12-27-virtual-dom-is-pure-overhead.md\\",\\"read_id\\":\\"430c3971b05d781d15c1246d6397dbca27ab8d1c47e2f04eee9fbf7c90bb0a83\\",\\"source_revision\\":\\"base\\",\\"source_sha256\\":\\"bd153122509e93817d8b6ffb21d54f01b458afdb4acef17b4660691fbcbe2255\\",\\"start_line\\":41,\\"total_lines\\":135,\\"utf8\\":\\"\\\\t<img alt=\\\\\\"Pete Hunt at JSConfEU 2013\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\